sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg critical wavelength for Drosophila persimilis at 2.1 µm faithfully reproduces Drosophila persimilis morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila persimilis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_persimilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila persimilis; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Noor et al. 2001: chromosomal inversions contribute to reproductive isolation between D. pseudoobscura and D. persimilis. | Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a cluster of incipient species. | Kambysellis et al. 1995: Hawaiian Drosophila diversified by ecological shifts; D. planitibia is the picture-wing successor in this chronoseries. | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: differential diffusion selects a finite critical wavelength. | Ready, Hanson & Benzer 1976: the retinal lattice motivates a period near 2 µm.; reconstructed_in_script: Onset wavenumber tuned so λ(D. persimilis) = 2.098 µm at r = 20, a = 0.10, b = 0.90. | λ(paulistorum) = 1.947 µm and λ(planitibia) = 2.735 µm from L^0.42, then integrated. Centroids 1.955 µm and 2.807 µm. | Du sweep Pearson r = 0.9993, RMSE = 0.033 µm. Ablation ratio = 0.051. Five-seed SD near 0. β endpoints 0.20 and 0.70 keep the predecessor shorter than the successor.; transfer_boundary: 2.098 µm is the assigned detail-tier wavelength (log10 = -5.678), not a numeral in the inversion paper. | Body lengths 2.36, 2.82 and 5.30 mm are catalog adult sizes. β = 0.42 is not fitted to a measured pigment series. | The GIF terminal frame is the gallery plate used by the image-fitness crop. It is not the Schnakenberg field.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery spiral is ocellar pigment at 2.1 µm. | Does not claim noise alone selects k_c in 1200 steps. | Does not reuse the 117 µm slot 2891 parameter table (alpha_scale 1.33).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(76)90225-6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/s0960-9822(95)00229-6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.221274498>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.45.3.419>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-persimilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

